      "type": "text",
      "text": "The five design specs are written and committed on `reqforge/TASK-0033` (commit `62d6758`). They aren't the original drafts from 2026-10-03: those weren't anywhere in the worktree, so I rewrote all five from the current code. Please review them as new content.\n\n**What changed:** five new files in `requirements/design/`, which is the `design/` folder of the requirements repository. Each starts with a `title` and a `realises` list:\n\n| File | Lines | Realises |\n|---|---|---|\n| `architecture.md` | 282 | REQ-0026..0029, REQ-0036, REQ-0046, REQ-0047 |\n| `data-model.md` | 361 | REQ-0003..0008, REQ-0035, REQ-0037, REQ-0042, REQ-0049 |\n| `api.md` | 330 | REQ-0013, REQ-0014, REQ-0020, REQ-0026, REQ-0027 |\n| `ui.md` | 318 | REQ-0030..0034, REQ-0045, REQ-0048, REQ-0050, REQ-0053 |\n| `agents-security.md` | 277 | REQ-0015, REQ-0040, REQ-0041, REQ-0047, REQ-0051, REQ-0052 |\n\nEach spec has a table of the requirements it realises, cites the source files it describes, and ends with an \"Open questions and gaps\" section. I replaced three made-up example ids in `data-model.md` (REQ-0056, STORY-0099, TASK-0099) with `NNNN` placeholders, because the Design tab would turn them into links to records that don't exist.\n\n**Checks I ran:**\n- **\"0 unknown realises ids\":** I couldn't check this with the real lint. reqforge doesn't read design docs yet; that's TASK-0034. Instead I ran my own script copying REQ-0054#AC1/AC2. It found 5 valid slugs, front matter in every file, and 0 errors: all 37 realises entries are existing requirements. Every REQ, STORY and TASK id in the text also exists, and the files are plain ASCII.\n- **E1** (`cargo test … --test integration -- design_docs`, built with `--no-default-features`): passed, but ran 0 tests (34 filtered out). The `design_docs` tests don't exist yet, so this proves nothing.\n- **E2** (`--suite design` end-to-end tests): not run. The Design tab is TASK-0035 and doesn't exist yet.\n\n**Still open:**\n- **Verify the specs:** E1 and E2 will only cover these files once TASK-0034 and TASK-0035 land. Re-run both then.\n- **List syntax:** I used block lists (`realises:` followed by `  - REQ-…` lines). The TASK-0034 parser must accept that form.\n- **Gaps the specs record:** the \"Open questions and gaps\" sections list places where the code falls short of the requirements. Among them:\n  - The routes that take a filesystem path don't validate it (TASK-0037).\n  - Chat MCP calls aren't tied to the chat's project, and the MCP server has no deny list of its own (TASK-0036).\n  - Changeset apply and CSV import are not all-or-nothing.\n  - The coding-agent sandbox only detects problems and doesn't undo them.\n  - Some features have no REST route, despite REQ-0026's \"every capability\".\n- **reqforge tools:** the reqforge MCP server failed to connect this session, so I read requirements straight from the JSON files.\n- **Google Calendar:** the claude.ai Google Calendar connector needs authorising in the claude.ai connector settings. This task didn't need it."
